From c04562b0dcb4a42d8797b446f897df55920a990d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:27:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8180x-xiaomi-book-12.4: add the EL2
 devicetree overlay

Qualcomm's hypervisor owns EL2 on this machine, so Linux normally runs in
EL1.  Secure-Launch (slbounce) can replace the hypervisor with Linux running
in EL2 -- losing its services, which makes a handful of device tree changes
necessary.  Follow the upstream "EL2 overlays for WoA devices" series and
express them as an overlay plus an -el2.dtb variant:

  * the GPU zap shader cannot be authenticated, so the adreno driver has to
    program RBBM_SECVID_TRUST_CNTL itself (and slbounce requires the node to
    be disabled to switch at all);
  * the SHM bridge to the secure world has to be self-owned in EL2;
  * apps_smmu reports 127 context banks in EL2 while the dtsi describes 106
    context interrupts -- without padding the list, arm-smmu fails its probe
    and every device with an iommu reference defers forever;
  * the ADSP/CDSP/SLPI, pmic-glink and LMH are firmware-owned and cannot be
    driven from EL2; leaving them described makes remoteproc shut the DSPs
    down, which resets the machine;
  * the videocc has no user on this board (venus is disabled).

Tested at EL2 on the Xiaomi Book S 12.4: EL2 with KVM (VHE), GNOME on the
panel, GPU firmware loaded, NVMe and eMMC both usable.

Signed-off-by: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile         |   3 +-
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-el2.dtso | 125 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 127 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8180x-el2.dtso

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
